  plain: `If you already use PostgreSQL, pgvector lets you add "search by meaning" without a new database: store each item's embedding in a column and ask for the closest ones using normal SQL.`,
  technical: `The extension provides vector types and distance operators (L2, inner product, cosine) with exact scan and ANN indexes (HNSW, IVFFlat). Benefits: transactional consistency, joins, filters and existing operations tooling; trade-offs: memory use of indexes, recall/speed tuning and scaling characteristics versus specialised systems. Version features (e.g. half-precision, sparse or binary vectors) change; check current docs and your managed-Postgres provider\'s support.`,
